Colibre Terms of Service (English translation; the Korean text above prevails)
Last updated / announced and effective: November 12, 2026. English pages: https://colibre.app/global/legal/

Run on support
   Colibre is made by an individual developer (Lee BumSuk) and run on support through Buy Me a Coffee (buymeacoffee.com). This is an early-access event before the official launch. Official sales are planned to start on 1 January 2027. Until then, supporters are given a 6-month pass. Support is voluntary. This does not oblige the developer to keep providing features, help or updates.
   If you have a pass code, enter it in the setup screen. The PC where the code is entered is unlocked for 6 months from the day the code was made (one PC). The pass is checked with the server (dd.colibre.app) when you enter the code and about once a week after that; if the PC cannot check for more than 30 days it locks for a while and unlocks once it is online again.
   Ask within 7 days of your payment and we refund your support through Buy Me a Coffee; after that, Buy Me a Coffee’s policy applies (Refund Policy). Send refund requests to support@colibre.app. Monthly support is charged automatically by Buy Me a Coffee every month and can be cancelled there at any time; cancelling stops the next charges.

What you may do
   The program is for personal use by the person who installs it, on their own PC, car and phone. There is a 10-day local trial from the first run; after that, playback other than radio stops. Official sales are planned to start on 1 January 2027. Until then, supporters are given a 6-month pass. To keep using Colibre after the trial, request a pass by email to support@colibre.app; passes are sent in order and may take some time. Colibre does not sell passes yet, because it is not yet a registered and certified business. Pass sales will start once registration and certification are done; until then Colibre runs on support only, as an early-access event before the official launch.
   Do not redistribute or resell it, decompile it or bypass its protections, share or publish your PC address or login, or use it for public broadcasting or commercial purposes. All rights in the program stay with the developer.
   The car-link feature is fully developed. Once service availability is confirmed, it will be opened after the necessary procedures; it is not available in this version. Separate terms and a location notice will apply when it is offered.

Your content, your responsibility
   Screen, media and radio travel only between your PC and your own devices, never through the developer’s systems. What you watch or listen to, and whether that respects copyright and each service’s terms, is your responsibility. Drivers must not watch or operate the screen while driving; while driving, listen to sound only (no video). The user is responsible for accidents and penalties caused by not following this.

No warranty · liability limit
   Provided as is, without warranty. It may stutter, lag or fail, and features may change or stop.
   The developer’s liability is limited to the amount you supported in the last 6 months. This does not apply to intent or gross negligence of the developer, or to consumer rights guaranteed by law.

Open source
   Bundled open-source components such as FFmpeg and Node.js follow their own licenses, and these terms do not reduce those rights. The list and license texts are in the licenses folder of the install. Modified FFmpeg source: https://github.com/sangre72/ffmpeg/tree/n8.1.3-17-d3d11fix-r3 — the source is also provided on request to support@colibre.app.

Other
   Everything that leaves your PC is listed in the Privacy Policy. Changes to these terms are announced on the website and in the program 7 days before they apply (30 days if they are less favourable to you). Korean law applies, and the Korean version prevails.

